{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs",
  "item": "mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Source-tool tests publish OutlineData addresses and retain mapped NodeIds\n directly in dependencies. This required Domain method is unused in\n those flows; stable-path and filesystem-storage tests use other domains."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]` meets the built-in's criteria.\n\n- **Placement and form:** It sits on an explicitly declared function with a body. The explanation is in fenced citation commentary, which counts as a tracked justification. It gives a substantive reason: `Domain` requires the method, but the flows in this test module never call it.\n- **Agreement with the source:** The test `Project` domain publishes `OutlineData` addresses through `source_node` and `source_address`. Its `ReadSource` criterion (`execute`) calls `cx.read_source`, which keeps `NodeId`s directly in dependencies. Its `outgoing_edges` returns an empty list, and its `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` ignore the node argument.\n- **Callers:** The only non-test callers of `Domain::node_path` are `edge_fingerprint` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs` and `prepare_edges` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs`, which reaches it through `edge_fingerprint`. Both call it once per edge target. `Project` has no edge targets, so they never call it. The tests that exercise `node_path` and storage use other domains: `ReviewDomain` in `graph/validation_tests.rs`, `Relationships` and `Application` in `tests/contracts.rs`, and `StoredGraph` in `tests/storage.rs`. The claim that stable-path and filesystem-storage tests use other domains therefore holds.\n- **Accepted assessment:** An independent assessment already exists in the `evidence/citations` records for this item.\n\nI found no gap.",
